    "sentence_translations": [
      "The “Big Three” in China’s Food Service",
      "",
      "No matter which town, district, city or province you go in China, ..",
      ".. almost every street is scattered with restaurants of different scales.",
      "The small ones are called fàn guǎn; the bigger ones are called fàn diàn;",
      "The cleaner and more modern ones are called cān tīng; the fancy ones are jiǔ diàn.",
      "Jiǔ diàn could also be hotels so you need to look into this before you get in.",
      "However, at present the “Big Three” in China’s food service, dominating towns and cities, are the following:",
      "Lanzhou Lamian (a.k.a. the muslim place), Shaxian Snacks and Guilin Mifen.",
      "They are everyday restaurants, convenient and cheap, enjoying great popularity among the public.",
      ""
